<PageTitle>Blazor Card, Card Group and Carousel — FlexCore</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Cards" Category="Components" ControlName="CardControl · CardGroupControl · CarouselControl"
                   Tagline="Show products, places or people as cards, in a grid or a carousel."
                   SourcePath="CardControl.razor; CardGroupControl.razor; CarouselControl.razor; CarouselItemControl.razor">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>CardControl</code> is a Blazor card: a bordered box with an optional header, image, body and footer for one item. Use cards for items users browse and compare: <code>CardGroupControl</code> wraps several in one <code>fx-card-group</code> element that you lay out with your own CSS, as the <a href="demo/cards#group">card group example</a> does with a wrapping grid of equal heights, and <code>CarouselControl</code> shows one card at a time, with arrows and dots to move between them.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="card" Title="Card with image, header and footer" RazorCode="@Code.Card" CSharpCode="@Code.CardCs">
            <Description><p>Send the quote from the card's footer and its badge and subtitle follow; pick an elevation to compare the shadows; None (<code>Elevation</code> 0) leaves only the border.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="demo-row">
                    <span class="field-label">Elevation</span>
                    <ButtonGroupControl Items="_elevationItems" Values="@(new[] { _elevation.ToString() })" ValuesChanged="PickElevation" AriaLabel="Elevation" />
                </div>
                <div class="card-stage">
                    <CardControl Title="Quote LIS-0001 Lisbon city break" Subtitle="@($"{(_sent ? "Sent to Albus Door" : "Quoted")} · 3 lines · $1,720")"
                                 ImageUrl="images/card-lisbon.svg" ImageAlt="Route sketch: airport, old-town hotel and food tour" Elevation="@_elevation">
                        <ChildContent><p class="m0">Return flights, four nights in an old-town hotel and a guided food tour.</p></ChildContent>
                        <FooterContent>
                            <BadgeControl Text="@(_sent ? "Quote sent" : "Quoted")" Variant="@(_sent ? BadgeVariant.Success : BadgeVariant.Info)" />
                            <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="@(() => _sent = !_sent)">@(_sent ? "Recall quote" : "Send quote")</ButtonControl>
                        </FooterContent>
                    </CardControl>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="group" Title="Card group" RazorCode="@Code.Group" CSharpCode="@Code.GroupCs">
            <Description><p>Pick a status to filter the quotes. <code>CardGroupControl</code> renders a plain <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>, so the example lays the cards out itself with one rule, <code>.quotes ::deep .fx-card-group { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }</code>, which keeps the remaining cards in equal heights and drops to two columns, then one, as the window narrows.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="demo-row">
                    <span class="field-label">Status</span>
                    <ButtonGroupControl Items="_statusItems" Values="@(new[] { _status })" ValuesChanged="PickStatus" AriaLabel="Status" />
                    <span class="result inline" role="status">@Shown.Length of @_quotes.Length quotes</span>
                </div>
                <div class="quotes">
                    <CardGroupControl>
                        @foreach (var q in Shown)
                        {
                            <CardControl @key="q.Name" Elevation="1">
                                <HeaderContent><span class="head"><span class="@q.Icon"></span> @q.Name</span></HeaderContent>
                                <ChildContent><p class="m0">@q.Summary</p></ChildContent>
                                <FooterContent><BadgeControl Text="@q.Status" Variant="@q.Variant" /></FooterContent>
                            </CardControl>
                        }
                    </CardGroupControl>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="carousel" Title="Carousel of destination cards" RazorCode="@Code.Carousel" CSharpCode="@Code.CarouselCs">
            <Description><p>Use the arrows, the dots or the buttons below, which call <code>Prev()</code>, <code>Next()</code> and <code>SelectSlide(0)</code>. Go to sets the bound <code>ActiveIndex</code> from the page, and Next on the last card wraps to the first.</p></Description>
            <Controls>
                <SwitchControl @bind-Checked="_showNav" Label="Nav buttons" />
                <SwitchControl @bind-Checked="_showDots" Label="Indicators" />
            </Controls>
            <Demo>
                <CarouselControl @ref="_carousel" @bind-ActiveIndex="_slide" ShowNavButtons="_showNav" ShowIndicators="_showDots"
                                 role="region" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="Destinations">
                    @foreach (var t in _trips)
                    {
                        <CarouselItemControl>
                            <div class="trip-slide">
                                <CardControl Title="@t.City" Subtitle="@t.Country" Elevation="2">
                                    <ChildContent><p class="trip-blurb">@t.Blurb</p></ChildContent>
                                    <FooterContent>
                                        <span class="trip-package">@t.Package</span>
                                        <BadgeControl Text="@($"{t.Nights} nights")" Variant="BadgeVariant.Info" />
                                    </FooterContent>
                                </CardControl>
                            </div>
                        </CarouselItemControl>
                    }
                </CarouselControl>
                <div class="trip-pager">
                    <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="@(() => _carousel!.Prev())">Previous</ButtonControl>
                    <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="@(() => _carousel!.Next())">Next</ButtonControl>
                    <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="@(() => _carousel!.SelectSlide(0))" Disabled="@(_slide == 0)">First</ButtonControl>
                    <span class="trip-count" aria-live="polite">Card @(_slide + 1) of @_trips.Length: @_trips[_slide].Package, @_trips[_slide].Nights nights</span>
                </div>
                <div class="trip-pager">
                    <span class="field-label">Go to</span>
                    @foreach (var (t, i) in _trips.Select((t, i) => (t, i)))
                    {
                        <ButtonControl CssClass="@(i == _slide ? "btn-sm btn-primary" : "btn-sm")" OnClick="@(() => _slide = i)">@t.City</ButtonControl>
                    }
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-cardcontrol-parameters" Title="CardControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Card.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="CardControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Card" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-cardgroupcontrol-parameters" Title="CardGroupControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Group.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="CardGroupControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Group" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-classes" Title="CSS classes" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Css.Length, "classes")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="CSS classes" Rows="Vocab.Css" />
                <p>Colors, padding and the three shadows are fixed in the stylesheet; it reads no <code>--fx-*</code> variables. Restyle by overriding these classes.</p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-carouselcontrol-parameters" Title="CarouselControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Carousel.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="CarouselControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Carousel" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-carouselcontrol-events" Title="CarouselControl events" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.CarouselEvents.Length, "events")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="CarouselControl events" Rows="Vocab.CarouselEvents" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-carouselcontrol-methods" Title="CarouselControl methods" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.CarouselMethods.Length, "methods")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="CarouselControl methods" Rows="Vocab.CarouselMethods" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-carouselitemcontrol-parameters" Title="CarouselItemControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Item.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="CarouselItemControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Item" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-carouselitemcontrol-properties" Title="CarouselItemControl read-only property" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.ItemProps.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="CarouselItemControl read-only property" Rows="Vocab.ItemProps" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-carousel-css-classes" Title="Carousel CSS classes" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.CarouselCss.Length, "classes")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="Carousel CSS classes" Rows="Vocab.CarouselCss" />
                <p>The carousel stylesheet reads no <code>--fx-*</code> variables either. The arrows (36px, 12px in from each side) and the dots (12px above the bottom) sit over the item, so pad the item's content to keep it clear of them; the example pads each slide by 64px at the sides and 44px at the bottom, or 56px and 40px on a narrow screen.</p>
            </DocSection>
        </DocSections>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <ul>
            <li><code>Title</code> renders as an <code>&lt;h5&gt;</code> and <code>Subtitle</code> as an <code>&lt;h6&gt;</code>; use <code>HeaderContent</code> when the page needs a different heading level.</li>
            <li>The image's <code>alt</code> is <code>ImageAlt</code>, then <code>Title</code>, then "Card image". Give decorative images an empty <code>ImageAlt</code>.</li>
            <li>A card adds no focusable elements of its own; links and buttons you put in the body or footer keep their natural Tab order.</li>
            <li>Unmatched attributes land on the root <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> of the card, the card group and the carousel. When the cards form a list, pass <code>role="list"</code> to <code>CardGroupControl</code> and <code>role="listitem"</code> to each card.</li>
            <li>Name a carousel with <code>role="region"</code>, <code>aria-roledescription="carousel"</code> and <code>aria-label</code>, as the example does. Its arrows are native buttons labeled "Previous" and "Next", and each dot is a native button labeled "Slide 1", "Slide 2" and so on, reached with Tab and pressed with Enter or Space.</li>
            <li>Only the current slide is rendered. Show the position in an <code>aria-live="polite"</code> element, as the example's count line does, so screen readers announce each change of slide.</li>
        </ul>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li>Badges, alerts, skeletons, timeline and breadcrumb: <a href="demo/new-components">UI elements</a>.</li>
            <li>Cards placed on a fixed grid of cells: the dashboard example in <a href="demo/layout#dashboard">Page layouts</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

